    {
      "id": "-8_KW8W4E9ak4Igip--HN",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -8878.030986023774,
      "y": -3627.2182849386936,
      "width": 1437.8181152343752,
      "height": 744.7020064562417,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "w2p0C7PxHocij1rwyX1el",
      "index": "b2HV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2017492183,
      "version": 1098,
      "versionNonce": 1701747836,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786078532696,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Must Signal: I have done ___ which resulted in ___\n\nKey Interview Questions & Their Hidden Meanings:\nTell me about yourself (1:00): Don't just recite your resume. Link your background directly to how you can solve the problem the employer is hiring to fix.\n\nWhy did you leave your last job? (2:06): \nEmployers are assessing risk. They want to know if you are a flight risk or if you tend to run away from challenges.\n\nExplain your job gap (3:19): \nThey want to know if there is a valid reason and, more importantly, how you stayed sharp and relevant during that time.\n\nWhat’s your greatest weakness? (4:12): \nThis tests your self-awareness. Pick a genuine, non-critical weakness and show how you are working to overcome it.\n\nWhat are your salary expectations? (5:04): \nA game of \"chicken.\" Be honest and provide a market-researched range to avoid wasting time.\n\nWhy do you want this job? (6:02): \nThey need to see genuine passion and mission rather than just a desire for a paycheck, which could signal you're a flight risk.\n\nWhere do you see yourself in 5 years? (6:41): \nA trick question to check for career alignment—does this role realistically lead to your goals, or are you just a temporary filler?\n\nWhy should we hire you? (7:50): \nYour final chance to demonstrate clear fit and present information that hasn't been covered yet.\n\nDo you have any other offers? (8:24): \nThey need to know if they need to expedite their internal process to stay competitive for you.\n\nDo you have any questions for us? (9:41): \nThis is for you to evaluate if the company is a good fit for you. Treat the interview as a two-way street.",
      "fontSize": 19.21811629564498,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Must Signal: I have done ___ which resulted in ___\n\nKey Interview Questions & Their Hidden Meanings:\nTell me about yourself (1:00): Don't just recite your resume. Link your background directly to how you can solve the problem the employer is hiring to fix.\n\nWhy did you leave your last job? (2:06): \nEmployers are assessing risk. They want to know if you are a flight risk or if you tend to run away from challenges.\n\nExplain your job gap (3:19): \nThey want to know if there is a valid reason and, more importantly, how you stayed sharp and relevant during that time.\n\nWhat’s your greatest weakness? (4:12): \nThis tests your self-awareness. Pick a genuine, non-critical weakness and show how you are working to overcome it.\n\nWhat are your salary expectations? (5:04): \nA game of \"chicken.\" Be honest and provide a market-researched range to avoid wasting time.\n\nWhy do you want this job? (6:02): \nThey need to see genuine passion and mission rather than just a desire for a paycheck, which could signal you're a flight risk.\n\nWhere do you see yourself in 5 years? (6:41): \nA trick question to check for career alignment—does this role realistically lead to your goals, or are you just a temporary filler?\n\nWhy should we hire you? (7:50): \nYour final chance to demonstrate clear fit and present information that hasn't been covered yet.\n\nDo you have any other offers? (8:24): \nThey need to know if they need to expedite their internal process to stay competitive for you.\n\nDo you have any questions for us? (9:41): \nThis is for you to evaluate if the company is a good fit for you. Treat the interview as a two-way street.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "w2p0C7PxHocij1rwyX1el",
      "type": "frame",
