    {
      "id": "0GN-o-SVepucuE7EYb7aH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -6616.11776183047,
      "y": -3970.149378271679,
      "width": 1196.3592529296875,
      "height": 1275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "w2p0C7PxHocij1rwyX1el",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1967602843,
      "version": 775,
      "versionNonce": 987606268,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786078532696,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Answer Framework\n• What was the project/problem?\n• What specifically was your role?\n• What technologies did you use?\n• What was the outcome/impact?\n• If limited experience: \"I haven't directly owned that, but I've worked with/alongside X and\nhave been building knowledge in Y.\"\n\nPython Experience\n• Be prepared with 2-3 examples\n\n• APIs, backend services, automation, integrations, data processing\n• Discuss architecture, challenges, and business impact\n\nFinal Reminder\n• Credibility > Perfection\n• Ownership > Buzzwords\n• Clarity > Overexplaining\n• Honest about gaps + ambitious about growth = strongest interview outcome.\n\n1. Situation, Task, Action Result\n2. Answer with specific examples of what i've done with concrete details leveraging the technologies used and their impact\n    2.1 Signal and narrate your resume's Google XYZ structure\n3. Audience must receive the signal you are prepared to do the job (not learn on the job)\n4. Philosophies of Code\n    - ...-driven-development\n        - business, test, type, domain\n    - assume users don't have ill-intent (happy path), minimum effective security\n    - leave code better than you found it, be empathetic to the developer who originally made it\n\nKey Coaching Point\n• Stay out of hypotheticals (\"I would...\", \"I could...\", \"I imagine...\")\n• Lead with what you have actually done\n• If you lack direct experience:\no Clearly state it\no Explain related exposure\no Demonstrate foundational knowledge\n\nPhrases to Use\n• \"My direct experience was...\"\n• \"I partnered closely with...\"\n• \"My level of ownership was...\"\n• \"I haven't directly done X, but I've gained exposure through...\"\n• \"That's an area I'm actively looking to deepen.\"\n\nPhrases to Avoid\n• \"I would...\"\n• \"I could...\"\n• \"If I were...\"\n• \"I've been exposed to...\" (without explaining what exposure means)\n• Any statement that blurs ownership vs participation",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Answer Framework\n• What was the project/problem?\n• What specifically was your role?\n• What technologies did you use?\n• What was the outcome/impact?\n• If limited experience: \"I haven't directly owned that, but I've worked with/alongside X and\nhave been building knowledge in Y.\"\n\nPython Experience\n• Be prepared with 2-3 examples\n\n• APIs, backend services, automation, integrations, data processing\n• Discuss architecture, challenges, and business impact\n\nFinal Reminder\n• Credibility > Perfection\n• Ownership > Buzzwords\n• Clarity > Overexplaining\n• Honest about gaps + ambitious about growth = strongest interview outcome.\n\n1. Situation, Task, Action Result\n2. Answer with specific examples of what i've done with concrete details leveraging the technologies used and their impact\n    2.1 Signal and narrate your resume's Google XYZ structure\n3. Audience must receive the signal you are prepared to do the job (not learn on the job)\n4. Philosophies of Code\n    - ...-driven-development\n        - business, test, type, domain\n    - assume users don't have ill-intent (happy path), minimum effective security\n    - leave code better than you found it, be empathetic to the developer who originally made it\n\nKey Coaching Point\n• Stay out of hypotheticals (\"I would...\", \"I could...\", \"I imagine...\")\n• Lead with what you have actually done\n• If you lack direct experience:\no Clearly state it\no Explain related exposure\no Demonstrate foundational knowledge\n\nPhrases to Use\n• \"My direct experience was...\"\n• \"I partnered closely with...\"\n• \"My level of ownership was...\"\n• \"I haven't directly done X, but I've gained exposure through...\"\n• \"That's an area I'm actively looking to deepen.\"\n\nPhrases to Avoid\n• \"I would...\"\n• \"I could...\"\n• \"If I were...\"\n• \"I've been exposed to...\" (without explaining what exposure means)\n• Any statement that blurs ownership vs participation",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b2L"
    },
    {
      "id": "SSg8TwEoGZEgn2xleju9E",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -8904.219479390917,
      "y": -4170.756702996978,
      "width": 923.3179582894181,
      "height": 66.15167348553688,
