      "updated": 1786677823502,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\"I am trying to better understand and gauge the level of functional code vs robust code and the culture design of code\"\n```python\ntemplate = [\n    \"example1\",\n    \"example2\",\n]\n\n?) is this the right data structure we should be using? is this OK now but for how long?\n\n\"\"\" psuedo code\ndef my_func() -> ?:\n?) data input, data type?1\n?) data output, data type?\n\n\nexplanation of the funcitonality of the code -> insight to where and how to define your naming convention\n\n\"\"\"\npseudoPayload1 = {\"example1-test\"}\n#pseudo_payload_2 = {\"example2-test\"}\npseudoPayload2 = {\"example2-test\"}\n\n\ndef my_func(\n    input_str_1: str, \n    input_str_2: str, \n    intput_str_3: str) -> None:\n\n \n    my_dict = {input_str_1: input_str_2}\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    #code compliles here in this script and runs\n    my_dict = {}\n    def my_func_list_of_str(input_str_list: List[str]) -> None:\n        #initiate my_dict where List[str] is just 2 elements\n         my_dict{input_str_list[0]}\n        my_dict[my_dict.key(0)] = input_str_list[1]\n  \n        for index, input_str in enumerate(input_str_list):\n\n        \n            \n    \n\n     \n\n",
      "fontSize": 17.421067915765406,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\"I am trying to better understand and gauge the level of functional code vs robust code and the culture design of code\"\n```python\ntemplate = [\n    \"example1\",\n    \"example2\",\n]\n\n?) is this the right data structure we should be using? is this OK now but for how long?\n\n\"\"\" psuedo code\ndef my_func() -> ?:\n?) data input, data type?1\n?) data output, data type?\n\n\nexplanation of the funcitonality of the code -> insight to where and how to define your naming convention\n\n\"\"\"\npseudoPayload1 = {\"example1-test\"}\n#pseudo_payload_2 = {\"example2-test\"}\npseudoPayload2 = {\"example2-test\"}\n\n\ndef my_func(\n    input_str_1: str, \n    input_str_2: str, \n    intput_str_3: str) -> None:\n\n \n    my_dict = {input_str_1: input_str_2}\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    #code compliles here in this script and runs\n    my_dict = {}\n    def my_func_list_of_str(input_str_list: List[str]) -> None:\n        #initiate my_dict where List[str] is just 2 elements\n         my_dict{input_str_list[0]}\n        my_dict[my_dict.key(0)] = input_str_list[1]\n  \n        for index, input_str in enumerate(input_str_list):\n\n        \n            \n    \n\n     \n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
